GET /orgs/{org}/rulesets/{ruleset_id}/history/{version_id}
Get a version of an organization ruleset.
Required: org (path) — The organization name. The name is not case sensitive.; ruleset_id (path) — The ID of the ruleset.; version_id (path) — The ID of the version

DELETE /orgs/{org}/rulesets/{ruleset_id}
Delete a ruleset for an organization.
Required: org (path) — The organization name. The name is not case sensitive.; ruleset_id (path) — The ID of the ruleset.

GET /orgs/{org}/rulesets/rule-suites/{rule_suite_id}
Gets information about a suite of rule evaluations from within an organization. For more information, see "[Managing rulesets for repositories in your organization](https://docs.github.com/organizations/managing-organization-settings/managing-rulesets-for-repositories-in-your-organization#viewing-insights-for-rulesets)."
Required: org (path) — The organization name. The name is not case sensitive.; rule_suite_id (path) — The unique identifier of the rule suite result. To get this ID, you can use [GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets/rule-suites](https://docs.github.com/rest/repos/rule-suites#list-repository-rule-suites) for repositories and [GET /orgs/{org}/rulesets/rule-suites](https://docs.github.com/rest/orgs/rule-suites#list-organization-rule-suites) for organizations.

GET /orgs/{org}/rulesets/{ruleset_id}
Get a repository ruleset for an organization. **Note:** To prevent leaking sensitive information, the `bypass_actors` property is only returned if the user making the API request has write access to the ruleset.
Required: org (path) — The organization name. The name is not case sensitive.; ruleset_id (path) — The ID of the ruleset.
